# /mot_nav_check: "can the dog do this?" asked of the SAME costmap and planner that drive it (one judge, P2).
# Waypoint k is an area (x[k], y[k], radius_m[k]). Optional taught path to waypoint k: path_x/path_y[path_off[k] : path_off[k+1]]
# (path_off has n+1 entries, or is empty when there are no paths).
# Checked per waypoint: inside the map; radius_m >= loc_sigma_m; the area is not mostly unknown; a usable position exists
# (a free cell with the hard clearance); it is connected to the previous waypoint (A*), or to the dog when use_start;
# a taught path keeps the hard clearance along its length.
float64[] x
float64[] y
float64[] radius_m
uint32[] path_off
float64[] path_x
float64[] path_y
bool use_start
float64 start_x
float64 start_y
---
bool available                        # false when no costmap has arrived yet (reason[] is then empty)
bool[] ok
string[] reason                       # "" when ok, else a short problem text
float64[] leg_m                       # length of the A* leg to this waypoint (0 for the first one without use_start)
# Geometry of those A* legs, for display only (the web console draws the later legs of a route): leg k is
# leg_path_x/y[leg_path_off[k] : leg_path_off[k+1]] (leg_path_off has n+1 entries; an empty range = no leg for that waypoint).
uint32[] leg_path_off
float64[] leg_path_x
float64[] leg_path_y
